This repository contains a UVM verification environment for the open-source
PCIe Root Complex of the openPCIE project (riscv_pcie_soc). Its own code and
documentation are licensed under the MIT License (LICENSE). It is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Chili.CHIPS*ba or NLnet; their names are used
here only to identify the design under test.

Third-party material
--------------------

1. openPCIE RTL (git submodule, not included)

   rtl/openPCIE -> https://github.com/chili-chips-ba/openPCIE
                   pinned at commit 6e48e11957e3f13494fbf6ffec91bfe2485d4e13

   Copyright (c) 2026, Chili.CHIPS*ba. BSD 3-Clause License (LICENSE.openPCIE).
   It is referenced by commit only and used unmodified. scripts/rtl_patches.py
   copies the files the testbench needs into build/rtl_patched/ and applies
   the patches listed by 'python scripts/rtl_patches.py --list'; the copy is a
   build output and is not committed.

   The openPCIE tree includes picorv32.v, the PicoRV32 RISC-V core
   (https://github.com/YosysHQ/picorv32), Copyright (C) Claire Xenia Wolf,
   ISC License.

2. Patches to the openPCIE RTL

   patches/*.patch contain lines of
   2.rtl/2.RC-direct.opensource/src/riscv_pcie_soc.sv from the commit above,
   with the changes this project proposes. They are derivative works of that
   file and are distributed under its BSD 3-Clause License
   (LICENSE.openPCIE), so that they can be contributed back unchanged.

No openPCIE source, RTL or generated output is committed to this repository
other than the patch context lines described in item 2.
